;; clojure-lsp configuration for glitter-gl.
;;
;; glitter-gl is a library, and its whole point is a public API other projects
;; call, not one this repo calls internally end-to-end. Without this,
;; `clojure-lsp diagnostics` flags every genuinely-public entry point as
;; "unused", which is wrong for a library and makes the linter noisy rather
;; than a useful signal.
;;
;; :source-aliases is pinned to #{:test}, dropping :dev from clojure-lsp's
;; default #{:dev :test}. clojure-lsp discovers the classpath by shelling out
;; to `clojure -A:<source-aliases> -Spath`, so the default made it run
;; `clojure -A:test:dev -Spath`. deps.edn's :dev alias exists only for the
;; co-development loop: it overrides the pinned glitter git coordinate back to
;; :local/root "../glitter", a sibling checkout that, as deps.edn's own comment
;; says, nobody outside the author's machine has. So on any machine without
;; that sibling the lookup died with
;;
;;   [ERROR] Classpath lookup failed when running `clojure -A:test:dev -Spath`.
;;   Error building classpath. Local lib io.github.jlt-commons/glitter not found: ../glitter
;;
;; and `clojure-lsp format --dry` exited non-zero. Found live: it passed on the
;; author's machine and failed on the first CI run, then reproduced exactly in
;; a fresh clone placed where no ../glitter sits next to it. Dropping :dev
;; costs nothing here, since :test is the alias carrying :extra-paths ["test"]
;; and is the only one clojure-lsp needs for source-path discovery.
;; :source-paths is pinned to include "examples" so the demos are covered by
;; `bb lsp:format-check` and `bb lsp:clean-ns-check`, and therefore by the git
;; pre-commit hook and CI. They were not, previously: clojure-lsp derives
;; source paths from the :extra-paths of aliases it recognizes, and while every
;; demo alias in deps.edn declares :extra-paths ["examples"], none of them is
;; named :dev or :test, so none was ever visible here. The 2026-08-07
;; project-wide format pass therefore reached src and test and left examples
;; untouched, and it had drifted by roughly 350 diff lines before anyone
;; noticed, because nothing was looking.
;;
;; Pinning the set explicitly also decouples this from deps.edn's per-alias
;; :extra-paths, so adding "examples" to some alias later cannot silently widen
;; or narrow what gets checked.
;;
;; Note that :source-paths and :source-aliases above solve different problems
;; and both are needed. :source-aliases decides the aliases in the
;; `clojure -A:... -Spath` classpath probe. :source-paths decides which
;; directories get analyzed. Setting one does not cover the other.
{:linters {:clojure-lsp/unused-public-var {:level :off}}
 :source-aliases #{:test}
 :source-paths #{"src" "test" "examples"}}
